-- title:
--   Normality of stalks of the base-changed Deligne–Rapoport model
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime with $5 \le p$ and let $\mathfrak X$ be a term of `DRModelPackage p`, i.e. a bundle of data and properties for the two-chart integral model `DRModel p` of the modular curve over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbf Z$ (properness, flatness and integrality of `DRModel.toBase p`, integral closedness of the sections over affine opens, models of the generic and geometric generic fibres with their compatibilities, two sections $\varepsilon_\infty,\varepsilon_0$ over the base, a smooth locus, and further data). Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain whose maximal ideal is generated by the image of $p$, and assume that the fibre product $\mathfrak X_O$ of `DRModel.toBase p` with $\operatorname{Spec}$ of $\mathbf Z \to O$ is an integral scheme. Let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$ and $\mathrm{to}\kappa : O \to \kappa$ a ring homomorphism. Assume the rationality hypothesis `hrat`: for every point $x$ of the fibre product of the two morphisms $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{compInf}\,\kappa$ and $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{compZero}\,\kappa$ into the base change of `DRModel p` to $\kappa$, there is a morphism $s$ from $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the residue field of $O$ to the base change of `DRModel p` to that residue field which is a section of the projection to the base, and such that the image of $x$ under $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{compInf}\,\kappa$ followed by the base-change map along $\mathrm{to}\kappa$ agrees, as a point of $\mathfrak X_O$, with the image of the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the residue field under $s$ followed by the base-change map along the residue map of $O$. Then for every point $x$ of $\mathfrak X_O$ the local ring of $\mathfrak X_O$ at $x$ is integrally closed.
--
--   This is the normality of the Deligne–Rapoport model of the modular curve after base change to a discrete valuation ring in which $p$ is a uniformiser, under the assumption that the crossing points of the geometric special fibre are rational over the residue field. It supplies the normality input to the construction of the resolved model, being used in [`ModularCurve.DRResolvedModelPackage.exists_isInvertible_and_pullback_toDR_iso_of_forall_exceptional_degree_eq_zero`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRResolvedModelPackage.exists_isInvertible_and_pullback_toDR_iso_of_forall_exceptional_degree_eq_zero).
